  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One turn",
      "items": [
        "A trigger on the glasses or phone starts a turn: one photo, one spoken question, transcribed on the phone",
        "The phone sends image and transcript to the gateway on the Mac; the answer returns on the same request and is spoken through the glasses",
        "Two things leave the private network, both from the Mac: the photo and question to the frontier APIs in phase 1, and read-only web requests from the harness lane",
        "The phone holds no model key. Keys for the frontier APIs live in the router on the Mac",
        "The Mac accepts nothing from the public internet. The phone reaches the gateway over the tailnet with a device token"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Frontier first, then local",
      "items": [
        "Phase 1 answers through the Claude API, the DeepSeek platform and OpenAI to set the quality bar",
        "Phase 2 moves routes to the Mac's local servers, Unsloth Studio and GLM on the DGX pair",
        "Switching is meant to be a route change in LiteLLM only; that is a design intent, not yet tested",
        "The four vendor clouds the old app called from the phone are no longer called"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Gates that stay with the operator",
      "items": [
        "Signing, App Store Connect, TestFlight and device registration",
        "Exposing the gateway on the tailnet, API keys and any router configuration change",
        "Purchases, sends to other people, deletions: never from a voice command"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What exists, what is planned",
      "items": [
        "Not built or not wired as of 2026-11-21: Xcode Cloud workflow, the app's move to the upstream base, wake trigger, turn engine, Reminders hook, harness lane, glasses gateway, turn log, Unsloth route, frontier routes",
        "Proposed, not yet decided by the operator: Xcode Cloud for build and delivery; Unsloth Studio as a phase 2 server",
        "Tagged configured: the router, local model servers, DGX pair, daily worker, vault and glasses exist per the operator's log or word; none was probed. The vault is the operator's current Obsidian vault, not the retired StudioVault repository",
        "Harness model calls are drawn through the router. A harness that can only call its vendor directly would be a third exit and is not used until that is drawn and approved"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Reading the lines",
      "items": [
        "Teal, thick: the path of one turn",
        "Pink, dashed: leaves the private network",
        "Purple, dashed: asynchronous or out of band",
        "Grey: supporting calls",
        "On a phone the cards read well and the map needs panning"
      ]
    }
  ]
